Rem Capability: terminal
Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedterminal.shoddy — reckoner seed: the console builtins
Rem
Rem PRINT, and only PRINT. The console has four builtins (terminal.shoddy
Rem documents them) and the other three read: Input and InputLine block
Rem for a line, InKey wants raw keys — all of them belong to whatever
Rem shell owns the session's input, and a dictionary word that read the
Rem console would fight that shell for it. Writing has no such quarrel:
Rem every shell already prints what a turn answers, and PRINT prints a
Rem little sooner.
Rem
Rem PRINT TOUCHES THE WORLD, and that is its whole point: it writes the
Rem session's output stream THE MOMENT IT RUNS, so a program looping
Rem with TIMES or FOLD can report each pass as it happens — where the
Rem stack's own display arrives only when the line finishes. What was
Rem printed cannot be UNDOne, exactly as a written file cannot.
Rem
Rem Strings print bare — "loop pass 3" PRINT says loop pass 3, no
Rem quotes, because PRINT's job is a report line, not a stack picture.
Rem Everything else prints as the stack would show it, at standard
Rem precision: the display format (FIX and friends) lives in the
Rem session state, and a touch word is handed cells, not the state.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"

Def TmSeedPrint(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "PRINT", 1, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => TmPrinted(vs)), "( x -- )", "Print x on the session's output, immediately — strings bare, everything else as the stack shows it, at standard precision.")

Def TmPrinted(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Print(TmShown(First(vs)))
    RckVals({ })

Def TmShown(c As Cell) As String
    Select Case c
        Case CutStr(t)
            t
        Case Else
            CutShow(c, CutFmtStd())

Rem ---- the seed -----------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedTerminal(st As RckState) As RckState
    TmSeedPrint(RckSeeding(st, "seed-terminal"))
